Type: Package
Package: stdd
Title: Stochastic Test-Driven Development for R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ed", "Phillips", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ed@phosphene.dev"),
    person("Jan", "Ritch-Frel", role = "aut"),
    person("Flow", "Feel", role = "aut", comment = "AI platform engineer")
  )
Description: Stochastic Test-Driven Development (STDD) utilities for testing
    probabilistic and Bayesian code. Standard deterministic assertions fail
    on MCMC, bootstraps, and other stochastic outputs. This package decouples
    deterministic math from stochastic simulation: controlled seed
    environments (with cross-platform RNG specification), parameter recovery
    tests (generate from known thetas, verify estimates fall in credible
    intervals), and convergence diagnostics (R-hat, effective sample size).
    Pure functional interfaces, no global state, one dependency (withr).
